<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Flow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        NEW FILE, 2026-09-01. Mirrors a principal's approval of an LOI__c record back onto its
        parent Opportunity, as part of W1 of the LOI approval cutover
        (agent-output/loi-approval-cutover-design.md). Direct sibling of
        flows/Underwriting_Approval_Sync.flow-meta.xml (2026-08-28) — same shape, same reasoning,
        different object. Read that flow alongside this one; where the two diverge it is called
        out below.

        🔴 THIS CONTRACT IS PINNED — the developer stream built LoiApprovalStampService to it; do
        not vary the action name or input variable name:
            Apex action:     LoiApprovalStampService (label 'Stamp LOI Approval To Deal')
            input variable:  loiId (Id)

        ENTRY — TWO SETTINGS, BOTH LOAD-BEARING (D-4, LoiApprovalStampService.cls's own header):
          - recordTriggerType = Update, NOT CreateAndUpdate. TestDataFactory.placeApprovedLoi
            INSERTS LOI__c rows already at LOI_Status__c = 'Approved'. Three of its callers insert
            251 rows in one DML (ContractExecutionServiceTest.
            bulkExecution251ContractsHandsOffToTransactions,
            .bulkExecution251AcquisitionPsasOpen251Offerings,
            ContractReviewTriggerHandlerTest.bulk251ExecutedContractsHandOff). CreateAndUpdate
            would fire this flow on every one of those inserts.
          - doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria = true. Two of those same three test methods
            THEN update those same 251 rows again (Stage__c -> 'Signed') while LOI_Status__c stays
            unchanged at 'Approved'. Without this setting that second save would still match the
            filter and fire the flow a second time — 251 more Opportunity saves cascading into a
            test that is measuring a governor budget.
          With both set, no existing fixture, seed or production path produces the TRANSITION: the
          only other production writers of LOI_Status__c are CounterOfferService ('Countered') and
          ApprovalAuditService ('Approved', but only downstream of THIS write, so no loop).

        🔴 NO REJECTED BRANCH. Per user decision D-3 (quoted verbatim in
        workflows/LOI__c.workflow-meta.xml and LoiApprovalStampService.cls), LOI_Status__c never
        moves to a value this flow's filter would see on rejection — the approval process has no
        finalRejectionActions at all, and Stage__c stays at 'Under Review'. This is not an
        oversight; there is nothing here to add.

        🔴 runInMode = SystemModeWithoutSharing, MATCHING Underwriting_Approval_Sync. This flow
        runs as the APPROVER, who is READ-ONLY on Opportunity and does not own the deal (measured:
        DPEG_Acquisition_View carries Opportunity with allowEdit=false / modifyAllRecords=false;
        ApprovalAuditService's header records the same finding from production). Without
        SystemModeWithoutSharing on the flow the downstream write has, in this project's own
        measured history, silently done nothing.

        🔴 THE PARENT WRITE IS DONE IN APEX (LoiApprovalStampService), NOT IN A FLOW recordUpdate.
        This repo has measured that SystemModeWithoutSharing on the FLOW does not, by itself, lift
        the access mode far enough for a read-only, non-owning approver's write to stick —
        AccessLevel.SYSTEM_MODE combined with a `without sharing` writer must be stated at the DML
        itself (see LoiApprovalStampService.cls's ParentStampWriter). Routing through the proven
        Apex path also keeps the "ONE DML, ONE field" contract in one place, matching
        Underwriting_Approval_Sync's own reasoning for why a second, later write on the same
        transition would be wrong.

        ⚠ DO NOT ADD ANY OTHER PARENT WRITE TO THIS FLOW. flows/LOI_Approval_Stamp (the existing,
        UNCHANGED, Opportunity-side after-save flow — entry LOI_Approved__c EqualTo true,
        doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria) depends on the mirror stamp landing in exactly one
        Opportunity DML so its own entry filter sees the transition. A second write here would
        consume that transition before LOI_Approval_Stamp's filter can see it.

        DEPLOY ORDER. This flow depends on LoiApprovalStampService (Apex, developer stream) and
        workflows/LOI__c.workflow-meta.xml (the field update that drives its own entry filter)
        landing in the same deploy — the actionCalls below resolve the Apex action by name at
        deploy/activation time.
    -->
    <actionCalls>
        <name>Stamp_LOI_Approval</name>
        <label>Stamp LOI Approval To Deal</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>134</locationY>
        <actionName>LoiApprovalStampService</actionName>
        <actionType>apex</actionType>
        <flowTransactionModel>CurrentTransaction</flowTransactionModel>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>loiId</name>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <nameSegment>LoiApprovalStampService</nameSegment>
    </actionCalls>
    <apiVersion>67.0</apiVersion>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <interviewLabel>LOI Approval Sync {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>LOI Approval Sync</label>
    <processType>AutoLaunchedFlow</processType>
    <runInMode>SystemModeWithoutSharing</runInMode>
    <start>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Stamp_LOI_Approval</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria>true</doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>LOI_Status__c</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Approved</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <object>LOI__c</object>
        <recordTriggerType>Update</recordTriggerType>
        <triggerType>RecordAfterSave</triggerType>
    </start>
    <status>Active</status>
</Flow>
